                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5096b7d0-5ffc-3d3b-aa4e-36e0268f2e06",
                        "entry_id": "a790f4bb-2591-3b0f-8c39-4e487aa1412a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A function (of time), denoted H, that corresponds to the total energy of the system."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a79acced-b23f-4ac8-88a5-a1af7a499a19",
                                "sense_id": "5096b7d0-5ffc-3d3b-aa4e-36e0268f2e06",
                                "text": "We contrast this with the case of sampling from the output of a quantum computer running the Quantum Adiabatic Algorithm (QADI) with the restriction that the Hamiltonian that governs the evolution is gapped and stoquastic."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2d59914-a08b-48b3-b6fc-a309ff3bbabb",
                                "sense_id": "5096b7d0-5ffc-3d3b-aa4e-36e0268f2e06",
                                "text": "As stoquastic problems we use frustrated Ising Hamiltonians, having random local X and Z ﬁelds, and random σ_zσ_z couplings."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cff33c9c-90bf-3b7a-873b-06d46633acd3",
                        "entry_id": "a790f4bb-2591-3b0f-8c39-4e487aa1412a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The observable, denoted H, that corresponds to the total energy of the system."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
